      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2021-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(\\sqrt{u^2}=|u|,\\) the expression equals \\[|3-2\\sqrt3|+|3+2\\sqrt3|.\\] Since \\(2\\sqrt3>3,\\) this becomes \\[(2\\sqrt3-3)+(3+2\\sqrt3)=4\\sqrt3.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Remember that \\(\\sqrt{u^2}=|u|\\)",
        "Decide the signs of \\(3-2\\sqrt3\\) and \\(3+2\\sqrt3\\) separately"
      ],
